 {
  "ticket_request": "Create code for moving proposal form for Vice President client",
  "final_answer": "To create the code for a moving proposal form for the Vice President client, we will need to design a form with fields for the necessary details. Here's a basic example in HTML and JavaScript:",
  "reasoning": "The request is for creating code for a moving proposal form. The solution provided is a simple example of how to create such a form using HTML and JavaScript.",
  "predicted_category": "Custom Development",
  "resolution_steps": [
    "Create an HTML file with form elements for the necessary details (e.g., name, email, moving date, etc.).",
    "Add JavaScript to handle form submission and validation.",
    "Style the form using CSS to make it visually appealing.",
    "Save the form as an .html file and share it with the Vice President client."
  ],
  "escalation_flags": {
    "needs_human": false,
    "needs_llm_escalation": false,
    "policy_gap": false,
    "reasons": []
  }
}

Here's a simple example of the HTML code for the form:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Moving Proposal Form</title>
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <h1>Moving Proposal Form</h1>
  <form id="movingForm">
    <label for="name">Name:</label>
    <input type="text" id="name" required>
    <br>
    <label for="email">Email:</label>
    <input type="email" id="email" required>
    <br>
    <label for="movingDate">Moving Date:</label>
    <input type="date" id="movingDate" required>
    <br>
    <button type="submit">Submit</button>
  </form>
  <script src="script.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

And here's a simple example of the JavaScript code for handling form submission and validation:

```javascript
document.getElementById('movingForm').addEventListener('submit', function(event) {
  event.preventDefault();

  const name = document.getElementById('name').value;
  const email = document.getElementById('email').value;
  const movingDate = document.getElementById('movingDate').value;

  if (name && email && movingDate) {
    alert(`Name: ${name}\nEmail: ${email}\nMoving Date: ${movingDate}`);
  } else {
    alert('Please fill in all required fields.');
  }
});
```

